 `sklearn/utils/_array_api.py`: This file contains the `get_namespace` utility function that provides the array namespace context. We need to ensure this function remains accessible since it's used to provide the `xp` parameter to both `_check_reg_targets` and `_find_matching_floating_dtype`.\n\n5. `sklearn/utils/__init__.py`: May need updates if the new internal helper function `_check_reg_targets_and_dtype` is created, although based on the proposal, this might not be necessary as the change can be made within the existing `_check_reg_targets` function.\n\nThe key modifications will involve:\n1. Adding dtype parameter to _check_reg_targets function\n2. Modifying the function to call _find_matching_floating_dtype internally\n3. Updating the return values to include the calculated dtype\n4. Ensuring proper handling of the array namespace (xp) parameter\n\nThe changes will allow the floating-point type checking logic to be consolidated into a single function, reducing redundancy across multiple regression metrics implementation files.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDaLIC raw evidence tools remain available throughout the investigation.\nIf your current evidence is either too broad, too few or incomplete, call `get_trace_artifacts` or `get_trace_data_dependencies` again with more precise